OSS wrote:
> Hi, All!
> I've been playing Nethack for about a year, but I'm ...a complete
> newbie at the moment. In most  of my games I clean out the mines and
> comlete the Sokoban, and then I get killed in a way most cruel ;)
> I wanted to ask you a couple of questions, the first of them being:
> 1. How do you heal yourself? I mean, you can just rest (space+numpad5),
> but that's time-consuming, ineffective and dangerous. You can also use
> a potion, but there's never enough of them. So, how a Real Nethack
> Player ;) should do it?

Once you level up a bit, you heal much faster.  If you're in dire
straits, retreat up the dungeon to heal--instead of sitting where you
are resting, run to the upstairs, go up, run to the upstairs, go up,
etc.  The monsters generated on shallower dungeon levels are weaker.

Primarily, try to avoid getting so injured that you need to heal.  Use
E to keep monsters from hitting you if needed, collect enough missile
weapons to kill from a distance, use choke points to avoid multiple
adjacent monsters if you must melee.

> 2. How do you kill cockatrices? Their "touch" effect almost always
> petrifies my characters, even though they(characters) wear full sets of
> armor, etc. How do I kill them? Genocide, maybe?

1. Make sure you have magic cancellation at level 3, that stops 98% of
touch stoning (and lots of other nastiness-level draining in
particular, also poison bites/stings and a bunch of other stuff).
Usually an elven cloak or mithril coat is the easiest way to get MC3,
normally you'll eventually want one of the other MC3 cloaks (robe,
CoMagicResistance, oilskin cloak, CoProtection).
2. Always carry a lizard corpse in main inventory (not inside a bag).
Actually, carry a few if needed.  Eating even a bite of it stops
stoning dead, as do acidic corpses (acid blob, black naga, etc) and
potions of acid (the latter are important for vegetarians).  The lizard
corpse (but not the others) will also stop their hiss stoning attack
from working 29/30 of the time.



